      "question": {
        ":question/id": "715a8ac6-fd66-549a-b175-7f154dd14992",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x) = 7{e}^{x} - 2{x}^{2} + 1$, find $f^{\u2032}(x)$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7{e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+1) \\\\ & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7{e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ & =7\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ & =7{e}^{x}-2(2x)+0 \\\\ & =7{e}^{x}-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
