        ":question/problem": "Given that $g(x)=4{e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+6x+8$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+6x+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8) \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-2(2x)+6(1)+0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-4x+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(4{e}^{x}-4x+6)\\,|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =4{e}^{0}-4\\cdot 0+6 \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+0+6 \\\\  & =4+6 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
